# Gradle (anchored: an unanchored build/ once swallowed a Java package named build/, silently
# keeping a whole pipeline out of git). The root itself is not a build since 2026-09-06 (Village
# Jobs moved to its own checkout); /build/ stays anchored for the same reason.
.gradle/
/build/
mcp-toolkit/build/
# ...and the convention plugin's. `/build/` above is anchored to the repo root, so every
# ADDITIONAL build root in this tree needs its own line.
gradle-conventions/build/
# The throwaway NeoForge spike (mcp-toolkit/docs/platform/CROSS_LOADER_DESIGN.md §11) is a build root too.
spike-neoforge/build/

# Game working directories (worlds, logs, downloaded assets, live resource packs)
run/
# mcp-toolkit is its own build root and hosts its own runServer; Loom needs a game directory
# that is NOT run/ because a dev client holds run/logs/latest.log open.
run-server/
# ...and any second server cell: `:runServer -PrunDir=../run-server-<name>` (0.89.0), which is
# how a session boots beside a live one — two servers on one run dir die on DirectoryLock.
run-server-*/

# Node
node_modules/

# Per-world agent memory (default root when MCPTK_MEMORY_DIR is unset) — world state, not source
mcp-server/memory-data/

# Experiment output (step-7 ablation grids, step-8 soaks) — data, not source; verdicts live in
# mcp-toolkit/docs/bench/ABLATION_RESULTS.md and docs/archive/COMPANION_DESIGN.md
mcp-server/ablation-results/
mcp-server/testbench-results/
mcp-server/testbench-results-aborted/
mcp-server/companion-results/
mcp-server/companion-soak-console.log

# Vanilla decompiled source, extracted from Loom's decompile cache by tools/extract-vanilla-src.ps1
# so Grep/Read work on it — derived data, regenerate anytime
/vanilla-src/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
mcp-server/testbench-run.log

# stray swap-experiment run logs
mcp-server/testbench-swap*.log

# stray bench run logs
mcp-server/bench-*.log

# probe battery run logs (tools/battery.ps1) — regenerated per run, cited by date not by file
mcp-server/sequential-*.log
mcp-server/battery-*.log
mcp-server/*.tap.txt
# ...and the rest of a battery's droppings, which the four lines above kept missing: the resume
# loop's bookkeeping (tools/battery-resume.ps1), the one-off recheck logs a red file leaves, and a
# whole run moved into a directory of its own so the next arm could resume from a clean one (the
# 2026-09-10 fabric-api arm, RELEASE.md 2.8 — a nested path the sequential-*.log pattern cannot see)
mcp-server/battery-*/
mcp-server/sequential-*-loop.txt
mcp-server/sequential-*.RESUME-DONE
mcp-server/*-recheck*.log
mcp-server/agentclient-*.log
mcp-server/chunkcheck.log
mcp-server/smoke-*.log

# console captures of a battery run (redirected by hand while running it from cmd.exe) - the LOGS
# under mcp-server/ above are the run's record; these are the terminal's copy of it
mcp-toolkit/logs/

# The world-model research project is ITS OWN REPOSITORY as of 2026-08-30, nested here rather than
# relocated: three battery probes (site-map, clinic-conformance, clinic-dry) resolve it by relative
# path, and the dev recorder's default data directory is <gameDir>/../world-model/data, so moving the
# folder would break working things for a cosmetic gain. Ignoring the whole directory is what makes
# the separation real - the workbench tracks not one file under it (96 files that predated this rule
# were untracked with `git rm --cached` on 2026-09-06), so nothing built or published from this repo
# can carry the corpus, the models or the research plans with it.
#
# Its own .gitignore carries the recorder-output rules that used to live here (data/, .venv/,
# __pycache__, .pytest_cache, *.egg-info).
/world-model/

# place_shapes measurement (mcp-server/measurements/): keep rows.jsonl + manifest.json + REPORT.md —
# they are the evidence and `run-shapebatch.mjs --from <dir>` re-derives the whole report from them.
# The raw per-turn sdk logs and tool transcripts are bulk, and testbench-results/ does not track its
# equivalents either.
mcp-server/measurements/*/sdk-*.jsonl
mcp-server/measurements/*/transcript-*.jsonl
mcp-server/measurements/*/nomem/

# Claude Code per-machine state: the permission allowlist is this machine's, not the project's;
# STOP_OK and the scheduled-tasks lock are runtime. A shared .claude/settings.json would be tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/STOP_OK
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# generated by mcp-server/probes/create-world.test.mjs at run time
mcp-server/probes/fixtures/k2-not-a-pack/
